# iOS MGL (OpenGL-on-Metal) — rebuildable vendor (2026-09-04)

The iOS GL path is MGL (`openglonmetal/MGL`, Apache-2.0): OpenGL 4.6/ES over
Metal, because EAGL/OpenGLES drawables are dead on iOS 26/27. The engine's GL
calls are translated at runtime GLSL -> glslang -> SPIR-V -> SPIRV-Cross MSL ->
Metal, with MGL statically linked into the app.

## Why this directory exists

The original MGL fork lived ONLY in `/tmp/mgl` (sources, iosbuild wrapper,
5 staged `.a`). `/tmp` was wiped -> the iOS build could not be relinked and
the fork was unrecoverable. This directory makes the build reproducible:

- `libs/`       the 5 static archives the engine links (committed; relink
                works offline). libmgl.a = MGL + SPIRV-Cross merged.
- `iosbuild/`   build script + toolchain + iOS caps stub + mach shim
- `mgl-ios.patch` iOS portability patch series on stock MGL master
- `README`      this file
- `../../ios-project/rebuild_ios.sh`  one-shot rebuild + relink + install

## Rebuild from source

Needs Xcode 27+, cmake, ninja, network (fetches MGL master + glslang +
SPIRV-Tools + SPIRV-Cross + SPIRV-Headers into `./work/`, gitignored):

    iosbuild/build.sh            # -> libs/*.a (arm64 iphonesimulator)
    ../../ios-project/rebuild_ios.sh --run   # rebuild app + install + launch

Expected output archives in `libs/`:
libmgl.a, libglslang.a, libSPIRV.a, libSPIRV-Tools.a,
libglslang-default-resource-limits.a.

## iOS patches on stock master (mgl-ios.patch)

- `MGLRenderer.h/.m`: TARGET_OS_IPHONE — UIKit vs AppKit;
  `CppCreateMGLRendererAndBindToUIView(ctx, uiview, contentsScale)` adopting
  the SDL_Metal UIView's CAMetalLayer; iOS `CppCreateMGLRendererHeadless`;
  CGRect-safe drawable code; `didModifyRange:`/MTLStorageModeManaged and
  macOS-only pixel formats guarded; Shared storage on iOS.
- `get.c`: `mglGetString(GL_EXTENSIONS)` returns "" (glad/`get_exts` queries
  it; NULL previously asserted in the default case).
- `textures.c`/`pixel_utils.c`: Depth24Unorm_Stencil8 is macOS-only ->
  Depth32Float_Stencil8 on iOS.
- New file `iosbuild/glm_params_ios.c` replaces `glm_params.c`
  (desktop-CGL dlopen): hardcoded caps max_texture_size=16384,
  max_3d=2048, max_cube_map=16384, max_vertex_attribs=16,
  max_color_attachments=8 + GL defaults.

Engine-side companion fixes (main tree, not part of the patch):
- `libs/pure3d/pddi/gles/glprog.cpp`: on iOS query `light0..3.*` uniform
  names (esToDesktopGLSL flattens the `lights[]` struct array — spirv-cross
  MSL cannot express it); SetLightState no-ops on absent locations (MGL
  asserts on glUniform(-1), GL spec says silent no-op).
- `libs/pure3d/pddi/gles/glcon.cpp`: `pglPrimBuffer::Display` rebinds
  GL_ELEMENT_ARRAY_BUFFER before glDrawElements (MGL tracks the element
  binding globally, not per-VAO).

## Caveats

- MGL upstream is a moving target; a newer master may need re-porting.
- `libglslang.a` ~88 MB; the 5 archives ~120 MB total (committed for
  offline relink; delete from git and rebuild if you want them leaner).
- Assets/sim facts (bundle com.c4rlox.simpsons.ios, sim iPhone 17 Pro
  UDID 969432DF-267F-4B28-8560-2502D085A3A6): see IOS_MGL_RENDER_HANDOFF.md.
